.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt KMSHAUNT.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kmshaunt.conf
.Nd configuration file for kmshaunt
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm kmshaunt
reads its main configuration from
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt/kmshaunt.conf
and a per-seat configuration from
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt/<seat>.seat.conf ,
normally
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt/seat0.seat.conf .
The directory is taken from
.Fl -configdir
(short form
.Fl c )
and defaults to
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt .
Both files are optional.
.Pp
The file contains the same options as the command line, written without the
leading dashes.
Only long option names are keys; the short command-line letters are not
recognized in the file.
Attributes that are lists on the command line, such as
.Cm mode
and
.Cm screen ,
are repeatable lines in the file.
.Ss File Syntax
.Bl -bullet
.It
The file is read line by line.
Each non-empty line is either
.Cm key
or
.Cm key Ns = Ns Ar value .
.It
A
.Cm #
starts a comment that runs to the end of the line, both in a key and in a
value.
.It
Leading and trailing spaces, tabs and carriage returns are removed from the
key and from the value, so blanks around the equals sign are insignificant.
Whitespace inside a value is preserved, except after a comma in a color.
.It
Boolean keys take no value.
Write
.Cm mouse
to enable an option and
.Cm no-mouse
to disable it;
.Cm mouse Ns = Ns Cm 1
is an error.
The
.Cm no-
prefix is recognized for every key, but only boolean options act on it.
.It
An empty value after the equals sign is passed to the option as an empty
string; boolean keys still reject any value.
.It
A key that runs to end of file without a newline, a
.Cm #
or an equals sign is an error.
.It
Unknown keys are reported and skipped.
A missing file is not an error; a file that exists but cannot be read is.
.It
A value that cannot be parsed makes loading the whole file fail, and
.Nm kmshaunt
reports that it cannot load its configuration.
.It
If a key appears more than once, the last value wins, except
.Cm mode
and
.Cm screen ,
which accumulate.
.El
.Ss Precedence
Configuration is applied in this order, later layers overriding earlier ones:
.Bl -enum
.It
Built-in defaults.
.It
The command line.
Every option set on the command line is locked and cannot be changed by any
configuration file.
.It
.Pa <configdir>/kmshaunt.conf .
.It
.Pa <configdir>/<seat>.seat.conf .
The seat file starts from the configuration produced by the previous step,
so it overrides the main file but not the command line.
.El
.Ss Value Syntax
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Boolean
No value.
.Cm key
enables the option,
.Cm no-key
disables it.
.It Integer
An unsigned integer, normally decimal.
Color components additionally accept a
.Cm 0x
hexadecimal prefix and a leading
.Cm 0
for octal.
.It String
The rest of the line, with surrounding whitespace removed.
Values such as colon-separated paths and comma-separated XKB options are
passed on as one string.
.It Color
Three components
.Ar r , Ns Ar g , Ns Ar b ,
each from 0 to 255, separated by commas.
Spaces after the commas are allowed.
Colors apply when
.Cm palette Ns = Ns Cm custom .
.It Login
The value is split into an argument vector with shell-like quoting, so single
or double quotes and backslash escapes preserve spaces:
.Cm login Ns = Ns \&"/bin/bash -i\&" .
.It Mode
An optional GPU and connector, the size and an optional refresh rate, for
example
.Cm card0[HDMI-A-1]1920x1080@60 ,
.Cm [DP-1]2560x1440
or
.Cm 1920x1080@60 .
The first matching entry wins, in the order GPU and connector, connector
only, then entries without either.
.It Screen
An optional GPU and connector followed by
.Cm normal ,
.Cm left ,
.Cm right ,
.Cm upside-down
or
.Cm disabled ,
for example
.Cm card0[DP-1]left
or
.Cm disabled .
The same matching precedence as
.Cm mode
applies.
.It Grab
See
.Sx Grab Syntax .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Global Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm help
Print usage information and exit (boolean, default off).
.It Cm version
Print the version and exit (boolean, default off).
.It Cm verbose
Raise the log level to INFO (boolean, default off).
.It Cm debug
Raise the log level to DEBUG and imply
.Cm verbose
(boolean, default off).
.It Cm silent
Only log warnings and errors (boolean, default off).
.It Cm configdir Ns = Ns Ar dir
Configuration directory used to find the seat files (string, default
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt ) .
The main file has already been located when this value is read.
.El
.Ss Seat Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm vt Ns = Ns Ar vt
Virtual terminal: a number
.Ar N
selects
.Pa /dev/ttyN ,
a value beginning with a period or a slash is a device path, and every other
value is prefixed with
.Pa /dev/
(string, default auto-detect).
.It Cm switchvt
Activate the VT at startup and restore the previous VT on exit (boolean,
default on).
.It Cm libseat
Acquire the seat through libseat, seatd or systemd-logind, instead of opening
the VT and DRM devices directly (boolean, default off).
.El
.Ss Session Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm session-max Ns = Ns Ar num
Maximum number of sessions, 0 for no limit (unsigned integer, default 50).
.It Cm session-control
Enable the session grabs; disabled automatically on real virtual terminals
(boolean, default off).
.El
.Ss Terminal Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm issue
Write the issue text to new sessions before login (boolean, default on).
.It Cm issue-path Ns = Ns Ar path
Colon-separated issue files and directories scanned for
.Pa *.issue
(string, default
.Cm /etc/issue ,
.Cm /etc/issue.d ,
.Cm /run/issue ,
.Cm /run/issue.d ,
.Cm /usr/lib/issue
and
.Cm /usr/lib/issue.d ) .
.It Cm asciicast Ns = Ns Ar file
Play the asciicast v2 or v3 recording
.Ar file
and stop at the first key press (string, unset by default).
.It Cm asciicast-loop
Restart asciicast playback when it ends (boolean, default off).
.It Cm login Ns = Ns Ar argv
Login argv (argument list), split with shell-like quoting (default
.Cm /bin/login -p ,
or
.Cm /bin/login
when
.Cm no-reset-env
is set).
.It Cm oneshot
Close the session when the login process exits and exit if it was the last
session (boolean, default off).
.It Cm term Ns = Ns Ar TERM
Value of
.Ev TERM
in every session (string, default
.Cm xterm-ghostty ) .
.It Cm reset-env
Start children with an empty environment and set only the session variables;
otherwise inherit the parent environment (boolean, default on).
.It Cm backspace-delete
Make the Backspace key send DEL (boolean, default on).
.It Cm sb-size Ns = Ns Ar num
Scrollback buffer size in lines (unsigned integer, default 1000).
.It Cm bell
Forward the terminal bell to the VT (boolean, default off).
.It Cm blink
Enable cursor and text blinking (boolean, default on).
.It Cm clipboard-read
Allow programs to read the console clipboard via OSC 52 (boolean, default
off). Denied by default: any program able to write terminal output could
otherwise exfiltrate copied text.
.It Cm clipboard-write
Allow programs to set the console clipboard via OSC 52 (boolean, default
off). Denied by default against clipboard poisoning; pastes are
safety-checked regardless.
.It Cm gui-osc
Honor kmscon's private
.Cm setBackground
/
.Cm setForeground
OSCs, which drop and retake DRM master for a GUI launch handoff (boolean,
default off). Denied by default: any output source could otherwise freeze
the display or steal DRM master from a running GUI.
.El
.Ss Input Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm xkb-model Ns = Ns Ar model
XKB keyboard model (string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-layout Ns = Ns Ar layout
XKB layout, for example
.Cm de
(string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-variant Ns = Ns Ar variant
XKB layout variant (string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-options Ns = Ns Ar options
Comma-separated XKB options (string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-keymap Ns = Ns Ar file
Precompiled keymap file, which overrides model, layout, variant and options;
an empty value disables it (string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-compose-file Ns = Ns Ar file
Compose file; unset or empty selects the default for the current locale
(string, unset by default).
.It Cm xkb-repeat-delay Ns = Ns Ar msecs
Delay before key repeat starts (unsigned integer, default 250).
.It Cm xkb-repeat-rate Ns = Ns Ar msecs
Interval between repeated keys (unsigned integer, default 50).
.It Cm mouse
Capture the pointer, enable selection with copy and paste, and scroll the
scrollback with the wheel (boolean, default on).
.It Cm natural-scrolling
Invert the wheel direction (boolean, default off).
.It Cm soft-cursor
Always draw a software cursor (boolean, default off).
.It Cm dpms-timeout Ns = Ns Ar secs
Blank the display after
.Ar secs
seconds without input, 0 to disable (unsigned integer, default 600).
.El
.Ss Grabs
A grab value is a comma-separated list of shortcuts.
Each shortcut is a sequence of modifier tokens followed by a case-sensitive
XKB keysym name, for example
.Cm <Ctrl><Alt>F1 .
Shortcuts and the matching rules are described in
.Sx Grab Syntax .
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm grab-scroll-up Ns = Ns Ar grab
Scroll the scrollback back one line (default
.Cm <Shift>Up ) .
.It Cm grab-scroll-down Ns = Ns Ar grab
Scroll the scrollback forward one line (default
.Cm <Shift>Down ) .
.It Cm grab-page-up Ns = Ns Ar grab
Scroll the scrollback back one page (default
.Cm <Shift>Prior ) .
.It Cm grab-page-down Ns = Ns Ar grab
Scroll the scrollback forward one page (default
.Cm <Shift>Next ) .
.It Cm grab-zoom-in Ns = Ns Ar grab
Increase the font size (default
.Cm <Ctrl>plus
or
.Cm <Ctrl>equal ) .
.It Cm grab-zoom-out Ns = Ns Ar grab
Decrease the font size (default
.Cm <Ctrl>minus ) .
.It Cm grab-session-next Ns = Ns Ar grab
Switch to the next session; requires
.Cm session-control
(default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Right ) .
.It Cm grab-session-prev Ns = Ns Ar grab
Switch to the previous session; requires
.Cm session-control
(default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Left ) .
.It Cm grab-session-close Ns = Ns Ar grab
Close the current session; requires
.Cm session-control
(default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>BackSpace ) .
.It Cm grab-terminal-new Ns = Ns Ar grab
Create a new session; requires
.Cm session-control
(default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Return ) .
.It Cm grab-rotate-cw Ns = Ns Ar grab
Rotate all displays clockwise (default
.Cm <Logo>plus
or
.Cm <Logo>equal ) .
.It Cm grab-rotate-ccw Ns = Ns Ar grab
Rotate all displays counter-clockwise (default
.Cm <Logo>minus ) .
.It Cm grab-reboot Ns = Ns Ar grab
Reboot the system, following
.Pa /proc/sys/kernel/ctrl-alt-del
(grab, disabled by default).
.El
.Ss Video Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm drm
Use DRM devices and ignore fbdev devices; when disabled, use fbdev (boolean,
default on).
.It Cm hwaccel
Use the DRM 3D backend and fall back to DRM 2D if it cannot be initialized
(boolean, default off).
.It Cm gpus Ns = Ns Ar list
GPU selection:
.Cm all ,
.Cm aux
(primary and auxiliary) or
.Cm primary ;
.Cm auxiliary
and
.Cm single
are aliases (enumeration, default
.Cm all ) .
.It Cm use-original-mode
Keep the current display mode instead of setting one (boolean, default off).
Cannot be combined with
.Cm mode .
.It Cm mode Ns = Ns Ar spec
Set a display mode; repeatable (mode list, empty by default).
.It Cm multi-monitor Ns = Ns Ar policy
Combine monitors with
.Cm largest ,
.Cm scaled
or
.Cm clone ;
unknown values behave like
.Cm clone
(string, default
.Cm scaled ) .
.It Cm screen Ns = Ns Ar spec
Set a display orientation or disable a display; repeatable (screen list,
empty by default).
.El
.Ss Font Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm font-engine Ns = Ns Ar engine
Font backend:
.Cm freetype ,
.Cm pango ,
.Cm unifont ,
.Cm psf
or
.Cm 8x16 ;
unset tries that chain in order (string, unset by default).
.It Cm font-size Ns = Ns Ar pixels
Font size in pixels, 0 to derive it from the display (unsigned integer,
default 0).
.It Cm font-name Ns = Ns Ar name
Fontconfig pattern, or a font file for the psf backend (string, default
.Cm monospace ) .
.El
.Ss Palette Options
Color values are
.Ar r , Ns Ar g , Ns Ar b
with components from 0 to 255 and are used when
.Cm palette Ns = Ns Cm custom .
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta=r,g,b"
.It Cm palette Ns = Ns Ar name
Preset:
.Cm custom ,
.Cm nord ,
.Cm solarized ,
.Cm solarized-black ,
.Cm solarized-white ,
.Cm soft-black ,
.Cm base16-dark ,
.Cm base16-light ,
.Cm vga
or
.Cm legacy ;
unknown names select the legacy palette (string, unset by default).
.It Cm palette-black Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 0 (black); color value, default 0,0,0.
.It Cm palette-red Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 1 (red); color value, default 205,0,0.
.It Cm palette-green Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 2 (green); color value, default 0,205,0.
.It Cm palette-yellow Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 3 (yellow); color value, default 205,205,0.
.It Cm palette-blue Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 4 (blue); color value, default 0,0,238.
.It Cm palette-magenta Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 5 (magenta); color value, default 205,0,205.
.It Cm palette-cyan Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 6 (cyan); color value, default 0,205,205.
.It Cm palette-light-grey Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 7 (light grey); color value, default 229,229,229.
.It Cm palette-dark-grey Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 8 (dark grey); color value, default 127,127,127.
.It Cm palette-light-red Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 9 (light red); color value, default 255,0,0.
.It Cm palette-light-green Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 10 (light green); color value, default 0,255,0.
.It Cm palette-light-yellow Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 11 (light yellow); color value, default 255,255,0.
.It Cm palette-light-blue Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 12 (light blue); color value, default 92,92,255.
.It Cm palette-light-magenta Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 13 (light magenta); color value, default 255,0,255.
.It Cm palette-light-cyan Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 14 (light cyan); color value, default 0,255,255.
.It Cm palette-white Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
ANSI color 15 (white); color value, default 255,255,255.
.It Cm palette-foreground Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
Default foreground; color value, default 229,229,229.
.It Cm palette-background Ns = Ns Ar r,g,b
Default background; color value, default 0,0,0.
.El
.Ss Grab Syntax
Modifier tokens are
.Cm <shift> ,
.Cm <lock>
(Caps Lock),
.Cm <control>
or
.Cm <ctrl> ,
.Cm <alt>
and
.Cm <logo> .
They are case-insensitive and must come before the key.
The key is a case-sensitive XKB keysym name such as
.Cm Up ,
.Cm Prior ,
.Cm Return
or
.Cm plus .
.Pp
A shortcut may list several keysyms separated by
.Cm + ,
as in
.Cm H+E+L+L+O ;
it then matches a key producing exactly those keysyms.
Several alternative shortcuts for one action are separated by commas.
An empty value disables the grab.
An event matches only if its set of the five modifiers is exactly the set in
the shortcut, so an extra held modifier prevents a match.
An unknown modifier or a keysym name in the wrong case is an error: the
option is ignored on the command line and aborts the file load in a
configuration file.
.Pp
Examples:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Reboot with Ctrl+Alt+Delete
grab-reboot=<Ctrl><Alt>Delete

# A Ctrl+Alt+F1 binding
grab-session-next=<Ctrl><Alt>F1

# Two alternative shortcuts for zooming in
grab-zoom-in=<Ctrl>plus,<Ctrl>equal

# A key that produces the keysyms H, E, L, L, O
grab-page-up=<Shift>H+E+L+L+O

# Disable scrollback scrolling with the keyboard
grab-scroll-up=
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kmshaunt/kmshaunt.conf
Main configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/kmshaunt/<seat>.seat.conf
Per-seat configuration file, normally
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt/seat0.seat.conf .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A minimal configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/kmshaunt/kmshaunt.conf
font-name=monospace
font-size=16
sb-size=10000
.Ed
.Pp
Use the Solarized preset:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
palette=solarized
.Ed
.Pp
Explicit custom colors; slots not listed keep their defaults:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
palette=custom
palette-foreground=131,148,150
palette-background=0,43,54
palette-blue=38,139,210
.Ed
.Pp
A German keyboard layout with custom repeat timing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xkb-layout=de
xkb-variant=nodeadkeys
xkb-options=ctrl:nocaps,compose:ralt
xkb-repeat-delay=300
xkb-repeat-rate=30
.Ed
.Pp
Two monitors with explicit modes and orientation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
multi-monitor=scaled
mode=card0[HDMI-A-1]3840x2160@60
mode=card0[DP-1]1920x1080@60
screen=card0[DP-1]left
screen=[eDP-1]disabled
.Ed
.Pp
A per-seat file that overrides the main configuration for one seat:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/kmshaunt/seat1.seat.conf
vt=3
session-max=10
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kmscon 1 ,
.Xr kmshaunt 1